   "body_md": "## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Fire On My Tounge**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 4 archived performances [5]\n- **In The Morning Liight**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [5]\n- **Taking Water- Ice Bridges**: earliest performance in the archive; mythic rare: 2 archived performances [5]\n- **Peach Pickin' Time In Georgia**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 3 archived performances [5]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **billystrings2022-06-30** (recommended): audience recording; 20 songs; 126 min [1]\n- **billystrings2022-06-30.travitz.schoepsCMC64v.flac24**: source not stated; 21 songs; 125 min [2]\n- **billystrings2022-06-30.travitz.schoepsCMC64v.flac16**: source not stated; 21 songs; 125 min [3]\n- **billystrings2022-06-30.schoeps_mk41_flac24**: source not stated; 21 songs; 125 min [4]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Stage talk about: Set One, Set Two [1]\n- The cover photo was taken from Ryan O'Malley's camera [3]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **billystrings2022-06-30**: taped by Marc Geanoules; transferred by Marc Geanoules; source: AUD->Sounddevices Mix Pre 6 [1]\n- **billystrings2022-06-30.travitz.schoepsCMC64v.flac24**: taped by Jeff Travitz; transferred by Keith Litzenberger; source: Schoeps CMC64v's>V3>SD744t [2]. Also: Recorded with Schoeps CMC64v microphones through a Grace Design Lunatec V3 preamp into a Sound Devices 744t at 24-bit/48kHz; Edited in Magix Soundforge Pro 16 for fades, split into tracks with CDWAV, encoded to FLAC with Trader's Little Helper, tagged in Foobar2000 [2]\n- **billystrings2022-06-30.travitz.schoepsCMC64v.flac16**: taped by Jeff Travitz; transferred by Keith Litzenberger; source: Schoeps CMC64v's>V3>SD744t [3]. Also: Same Schoeps CMC64v, Lunatec V3, 744t source chain; this copy was converted to 44.1kHz and 16-bit in Soundforge Pro 16, then FLAC encoded [3]\n- **billystrings2022-06-30.schoeps_mk41_flac24**: taped by Adam Blair; transferred by Andy Murray; source: Schoeps mk41>cmc1L>Sound Devices Mixpre 6ii 32bit/96khz [4]. Also: Schoeps MK41 recording processed in Reaper with fades, tracking, EQ, normalization and a Fab Filter Pro L2 limiter, rendered at 24-bit/96kHz [4]\n\n## Art and photos\n\n- Poster by @BillybaseDotNet: [Billy Strings Peach Music Festival - Scranton, PA - BillyBase](https://billybase.net/show/peach-music-festival-scranton-pa/) [6]",
